{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Ethan jolted awake to the cold, sterile glow of a loading screen—his name flashed in pixelated text: **\"ETHAN_CARTER, LEVEL 1.\"** His hands trembled as he flexed them, expecting flesh, but found only a controller-like interface hovering above his bed. The walls of his apartment dissolved into a blocky, retro-style landscape, complete with a health bar flickering above his head and a looming NPC in a tattered hoodie blocking the door. *\"You’ve been selected for a one-time quest,\"* a robotic voice announced. *\"Objective: Escape the Glitch Zone before the system resets.\"* Panic surged as Ethan’s fingers brushed against a floating inventory slot—his keys, wallet, and even his wedding ring were gone, replaced by a rusted sword and a note: *\"Real life was just a trial run.\"*\n\nAs Ethan sprinted through the game’s jagged terrain, he discovered others like him—players caught in the loop—whispering about \"the devs\" who controlled their fate. A glitch-torn forest revealed a hidden dialogue option: *\"Ask about the developer.\"* When he spoke, the hooded NPC’s face cracked like a corrupted texture, revealing a human behind the mask. *\"You don’t remember?\"* they asked. *\"You designed this. Every reset, you forget. But this time… the code has a bug.\"* The screen flickered violently as Ethan’s health bar drained, and the voice hissed, *\"Start over.\"* His fingers twitched toward the power button—except there wasn’t one. Only a single, blinking prompt: **\"CONFIRM LOAD?\"**", "logprobs": [{"token": "E", "logprob": -1.9033106565475464}, {"token": "than", "logprob": -0.011208427138626575}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.38688793778419495}, {"token": "olt", "logprob": -0.0007765853079035878}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": -1.5258672647178173e-05}, {"token": " awake", "logprob": -0.011262179352343082}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.26329132914543